#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=w:Peter F. Hamilton|title=The Dreaming Void|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=ku9OSCWRN7wC&pg=PT191&dq=%22bot%22%7C%22bots%22+-intitle:%22bot%7Cbots%22+-inauthor:%22bot%7Cbots%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=a78CT4k9o4qZBa3q5bQC&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22bot%22%7C%22bots%22%20-intitle%3A%22bot%7Cbots%22%20-inauthor%3A%22bot%7Cbots%22&f=false|passage=The '''bot''' juddered to a halt, as the whole lower segment of its power arm darkened.}}
# {{lb|en|computing}} A piece of [[software]] designed to perform a minor but [[repetitive]] [[task]] [[automatically]] or on [[command]], especially when operating with the appearance of a (human) user profile or account.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=Ryan Farley; Xinyuan Wang|chapter=Roving Bugnet: Distributed Surveillance Threat and Mitigation|editors=Dimitris Gritzalis; Javier López|title=Emerging Challenges for Security, Privacy and Trust: 24th IFIP TC 11 International Information Security Conference|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=3CzqIkb5JKEC&pg=PA42&dq=%22bot%22%7C%22bots%22+-intitle:%22bot%7Cbots%22+-inauthor:%22bot%7Cbots%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=hbsCT8SeMdCgmQWHyeiQCA&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22bot%22%7C%22bots%22%20-intitle%3A%22bot%7Cbots%22%20-inauthor%3A%22bot%7Cbots%22&f=false|page=42|passage=The goals of IRC '''bots''' vary widely, such as automatically kicking other users off or more nefarious things like spamming other IRC users. In this paper, a free standing IRC '''bot''' is presented that monitors an IRC channel for commands from a particular user and responds accordingly.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=Richard K. Neumann|title=Legal Reasoning and Legal Writing: Structure, Strategy, and Style|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=wxojAQAAMAAJ&q=%22bot%22%7C%22bots%22+-intitle:%22bot%7Cbots%22+-inauthor:%22bot%7Cbots%22&dq=%22bot%22%7C%22bots%22+-intitle:%22bot%7Cbots%22+-inauthor:%22bot%7Cbots%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=hbsCT8SeMdCgmQWHyeiQCA&redir_esc=y|page=91|passage=He is particularly good at creating web robots, which are also called '''bots'''. A '''bot''' is software that searches for certain kinds of websites and then automatically does something — good or bad — on each site. Google uses '''bots''' to search and index websites.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=Dusty Reagan|title=Twitter Application Development For Dummies|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=V_tf644oVQAC&pg=PA59&dq=%22bot%22%7C%22bots%22+-intitle:%22bot%7Cbots%22+-inauthor:%22bot%7Cbots%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=IbYCT4_HLsXJmAXkrNW1Ag&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22bot%22%7C%22bots%22%20-intitle%3A%22bot%7Cbots%22%20-inauthor%3A%22bot%7Cbots%22&f=false|page=59|passage=Twitter '''bots''' can leverage Twitter′s text message support to allow users to accomplish tasks from their cell phones. You could consider Twitter accounts that are simply an automated import of blog′s RSS feed a Twitter '''bot'''.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.theatlantic.com/technology/archive/2017/01/bots-bots-bots/515043/|title=The Internet Is Mostly Bots|date=2017-01-31|accessdate=2021-09-01|author=Adrienne LaFrance|work=The Atlantic|passage=Overall, '''bots'''—good and bad—are responsible for 52 percent of web traffic, according to a new report by the security firm Imperva, which issues an annual assessment of '''bot''' activity online.}}
# {{lb|en|video games}} A computer-controlled [[character]] in a [[video game]], especially a [[multiplayer]] one.
#: {{syn|en|NPC|AI}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Philip Hingston|title=Believable Bots: Can Computers Play Like People?|year=2012|publisher=Springer Science & Business Media|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=nR-hLzoyMnUC&pg=PA232&dq=bot+multiplayer&hl=&cd=7&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=bot%20multiplayer&f=false|isbn=978-3-642-32322-5|page=232|passage=Most games offer both single player mode, in which a player competes against computer rivals—'''bots'''—and a multiplayer mode, which is a contest among people only.}}
# {{lb|en|video games|slang|derogatory}} A supremely [[unskilled]] player.
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.eurogamer.net/call-of-duty-warzone-squad-sets-new-world-record-with-162-kills|work=Eurogamer|passage="That lobby was bronze negative 10!" Aydan joked on-stream, noting how easy it felt for his squad. "We got blessed with the lobby. It was such a '''bot''' lobby."|title=Call of Duty: Warzone squad sets new world record with an astonishing 162 kills in a single game|date=2021-03-06|author=Aydan Conrad (quoted); Wesley Yin-Poole}}
